    <bpmn:process id="W_W5030" name="W5030. Peer, Valuation-Multiple &amp; Capital-Structure Benchmarking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Valuation review; rating/cost-of-capital analysis; transaction (VS-130); strategic-plan refresh (VS-33)
Frequency: Periodic (quarterly) + event-driven
Volume: ~8–12 companies in the peer set × metrics × quarterly cycles
Owner: VP Investor Relations / Strategy (VS-33) / CFO
Participants: Strategy (VS-33), Finance/FP&amp;A (VS-17.4), Treasury (VS-18), Analytics (VS-28), ABL/Collateral (VS-170)
Source: workflow W5030 — Peer, Valuation-Multiple &amp; Capital-Structure Benchmarking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5030_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5030_Lane1" name="VP IR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5030_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5030_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5030_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5030_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5030_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5030_Start3" name="Valuation review; rating/cost-of-capital analysis; transaction (VS-130); strategic-plan…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5030_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5030_Task4" name="Build &amp; maintain the peer set: comparable…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Build &amp; maintain the peer set: comparable retailers/home-improvement/Philippine-conglomerate peers, the peer-group rationale, and the metric framework (revenue/margin/turns/growth, leverage, coverage, returns)
Responsible (R): VP IR / Strategy / Analytics
Accountable (A): VP IR
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5030_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5030_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5030_Task5" name="Benchmark valuation, multiples &amp; capital structure: BuildRight vs peers on…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Benchmark valuation, multiples &amp; capital structure: BuildRight vs peers on valuation multiples (P/E, EV/EBITDA-equivalent), capital structure &amp; leverage (debt/equity, coverage — links VS-18/VS-170), cost of capital, and rating posture (W5013)
Responsible (R): VP IR / Strategy / Treasury / FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): VP IR / CFO
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5030_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5030_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5030_Task6" name="Synthesize to narrative &amp; decisions: identify the valuation gap/narrative…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Synthesize to narrative &amp; decisions: identify the valuation gap/narrative levers (W5009), feed cost-of-capital/capital-structure decisions (VS-18/VS-33), and the equity story (W5009) and board reporting (W5024)
Responsible (R): VP IR / Strategy / CFO
Accountable (A): VP IR / CFO
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5030_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5030_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5030_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
